      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa3c44bb_c8d6232f",
        "filename": "src/MainNFSD/nfs_qos.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 379,
      "author": {
        "id": 1038286
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T16:19:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For freeing of client and export entries, QOS has exposed the same API, which based up on the path should be used.\nfor example, client path gsh_client should be passed and qos_class_type should be QOS_CLIENT, the same is applicable for export as well(gsh_export and QOS_EXPORT).\nit is just to keep same free api (i.e gsh_free_mem) for export and client.\nQOS will try to map it to where the memory needs to be freed from based on the current qos_type enabled.",
      "parentUuid": "a9e9c7ae_d8d06aaa",
      "revId": "110655858a554265dcda4558a55508a4c6297bd8",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
