      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:20:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So (mostly) export-\u003eqos_block is not referenced past the QoS_perExportInsert call?\n\nBut there are dbus commands that access it that could race with export update.\n\nSince qos_block is really only used during config and by those dbus commands, the cost of a lock is minimal.\n\nHmm, also QoS_perExportInsert can be called for I/O, inserting the global QoS per export params. That could race with an export update.\n\nHmm, suggest you just take the g_qos_lock for this function and in the dbus commands. That should protect everything with minimal lock contention.",
      "parentUuid": "d88214fe_6dc7ef73",
      "revId": "110655858a554265dcda4558a55508a4c6297bd8",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
